//? Title: Two-Stream:actual adjacent-frame flow and visible tensor optimizers
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Action classification needs appearance and motion information from original video. A middle RGB frame and ten estimated consecutive-frame flow fields feed complete CNN-M branches,with explicit fieldSGD and classifierAdam loops and every held-out error.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/two_stream.cpp`.

> The method

Two disjoint CNN-M models learn spatial and temporal evidence. Centering each signed flow field removes its spatial mean;interleaving its dx/dy components supplies20channels. The learning and inference rules differ:

$$ L=CE(z^{RGB},y)+CE(z^{flow},y),\qquad p=\tfrac12[softmax(z^{RGB})+softmax(z^{flow})]. $$
\alttext(The fitting loss adds two independent mean cross-entropies;inference averages the two independently normalized probability vectors.)

All preprocessing,forward,loss,optimization,inference,metrics and plot values use the tensor library. The declared flow-estimation adaptation is shown explicitly and is separate from the CNN fitting objective. Full reference geometry is an analytical census;both complete compact streams actually execute.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/two_stream_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/two_stream_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/two_stream_concept.tikz > build/two_stream_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/two_stream_concept.svg build/two_stream_concept.dvi > build/two_stream_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
